# LF in the repo and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. A browser text area hands back LF
# whatever it was given, and the app writes raw bytes. With Windows'
# core.autocrlf=true, git would hand out CRLF files and the first save
# through the app would rewrite every line - a whole-file diff nobody
# made. The eol=lf here overrides that per repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

